  "body": "﻿## What changed\n\n- Added `waterlines: bool` (default `true`) across `Finish3DParams`, `OpParams::Finish3D`, `ParamsDto::Finish3D`, MCP tools (`add_operation`, `edit_operation`, `list_operation_types`), project serialization (`#[serde(default = \"default_true\")]`), and the 3D Finish Passes UI tab (`Steep flanks`: `Waterlines` / `Leave uncut` with an inline consequence note).\n- Updated `rings_and_tail_with_trim` and `swarf_multi` so `waterlines: false` skips the steep-flank waterline ring pass on shallow-first patterns, emits a visible steep-flank note on `Toolpath::notes` (surfaced in the UI status banner and MCP output), keeps uncut steep-flank stock visible to downstream rest checks, and refuses all-steep or no-shallow-cut models with `GenError::Empty`.\n- Refused `waterlines: false` by name for ring-dependent patterns (`Waterline`, `Blend`, `Morph`), and hid the switch in the UI for patterns without a steep-flank waterline pass (`Waterline`, `Blend`, `Morph`, `Flat`, `Pencil`, `Corner`, `Geodesic`).\n- Split `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/validate.rs` from `params.rs` for the 400-line file rule, added pinning tests in `crates/motion/tests/finish3d_waterlines.rs`, `crates/app/tests/operations.rs`, `crates/app/tests/mcp.rs`, `crates/app/tests/project_roundtrip.rs`, and `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs`, and recorded design decisions in `docs/decisions/2811-finish-waterlines-switch.md`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- All checks below ran on final head `4cbefddf5143f96c37863af89ee7899c0f40821d` via separate `gate-runner`:\n  - `cargo clippy -j 10 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed (exit 0).\n  - `cargo test -j 10 -p camcraft-motion --lib --test finish3d_waterlines --test finish3d --test finish3d_gaplink --test finish3d_holes --test finish3d_land --test finish3d_overhang_and_chord`: 618 passed, 0 failed, 44 ignored (`finish3d_waterlines`: 5 passed; `--lib`: 536 passed, 10 ignored; `finish3d`: 55 passed, 33 ignored).\n  - `cargo test -j 10 -p camcraft-app --test operations --test mcp --test mcp_doc_drift --test project_roundtrip --test golden_cl --test verify --test area_controls --test setup_align_3d --test wcs_start --test posed_contact --test import_step_q02_mold`: 316 passed, 0 failed, 9 ignored (`operations`: 123 passed; `mcp`: 24 passed; `mcp_doc_drift`: 6 passed; `project_roundtrip`: 78 passed).\n  - `cargo test -j 10 -p camcraft-ui --lib -- --test-threads=1` (in `crates/ui`, single-threaded per Windows #3379): 1429 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored (includes `finish3d_waterlines_radio_consequence_apply_undo_and_status_note`).\n  - `cargo test -j 10 --release -p camcraft-motion --test finish3d_waterlines --test finish3d -- --ignored`: 33 passed, 0 failed (`finish3d`: 33 passed, 55 filtered; `finish3d_waterlines`: 0 passed, 5 filtered).\n- Trial merge against `upstream/main` (`43217a7c4`): clean (`git merge-tree --write-tree` exit 0).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Remaining `motion heavy` and `app heavy` lanes (242 steps in `cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run`): not run - owed to the wave run before merge (#3467).\n- Full `cargo xtask gate batch` across unrelated `camcraft-app` / `camcraft-ui` integration binaries.\n- Manual before/after desktop screenshots of the 3D Finish Passes tab.\n\nfork synced at v0.25.0\nChangelog: Added a Waterlines switch to 3D Finish operations to skip steep-flank ring passes with a visible uncut-flank warning and all-steep refusal.\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2811\r\n",
